docs/reported/carrier-sum-option-boxes-have-no-owner.md

The unpinned `(peek (ok 1))` hands its fresh 16-byte carrier box to a
COLORED callee.  elab_call.c stamps a fresh sum argument for the drop-after
free only when the callee has an EMPTY effect row (a suspended continuation
could outlive the call and read the freed box), so this one box is left to
the erased-residue category that report tracks.  The pinned calls beside it
are by-value and allocate nothing.
